# Without this file, `fly deploy` tars the ENTIRE repo root — .env with
# every live secret, provider session cookies, and 10 MB of recorded
# HAR/trace fixtures — and ships it to Fly's remote builder; the build
# stage's `COPY executor executor` would also layer the cookies into the
# builder cache. The Dockerfile's runtime stage copies an explicit
# allowlist, but the context and build stage must be clean too.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.git
node_modules
**/node_modules
executor/storageState*.json
executor/fixtures
executor/captures
**/dist
data
docs
ios
*.log
.DS_Store
.claude
